cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Explicit Hamiltonian ball packings in every dimension"
version: "1.2.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24209739"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-JoL/Symplectic-Ball-Packing"
authors:
  - family-names: Song
    given-names: Liang
    email: sl12160010@gmail.com
abstract: >-
  Uniformly for every integer k ≥ 10 (including all non-square values) and every ε in (0,1), we
  define one explicit smooth compactly supported Hamiltonian on R × R^4 whose time-one map carries
  the k closed unit balls centred at (3i−3,0,0,0) into the ball of radius (k/(1−ε/4))^{1/4}, with
  an explicit stability margin and formally verified perturbed fixed-step RK4 target containment,
  without J-holomorphic curves or Seiberg–Witten theory. The same construction realises every ball
  packing allowed by the volume and two-ball inequalities in dimension 2n ≥ 6, and every packing
  with Σc_i² < C² and 3c_i < C in dimension four, proving Biran's full-packing theorem for k ≥ 9
  equal balls. Includes four papers (equal balls in the four-ball, general capacities and higher
  dimensions with a uniform finite-output algorithm, elementary packings and their obstructions,
  and closed-form C^4 equal-ball embeddings with exact-real inverse certificates and stagewise
  Liouville generators), supplements, a Lean 4 formalisation, and two accompanying Python programs
  (an elementary-flow generator in Epoch's RK4 format and a modular closed-form C^4 embedding
  evaluator with 100-digit mpmath verification).
keywords:
  - symplectic ball packing
  - Hamiltonian dynamics
  - packing stability
  - explicit constructions
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
